[[build-shm]]
=== Shared memory layout

**STUB**: Specifies the shared memory that pools use to exchange large values
without copying. Defines volumes, the volume header, block headers, and the
three pointer forms (pool-relative, volume-relative, absolute) with the rules
for converting between them. Covers allocation, reference counting and release,
how volumes are created and attached safely by concurrent processes, and how
file locking protects them.

